      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\n`_get_new_batch_prefill_raw()` has two branches: the mixed-chunk branch filters `running_batch` before mixing it into the prefill batch, while the `else` branch leaves `running_batch` untouched. A request that lands in `running_batch` is then only ever removed by `update_running_batch()`, which runs exclusively on the decode path — and under chunked prefill that path is starved, because a chunked prefill is essentially always in progress and `_get_new_batch_prefill_raw` keeps producing prefill batches.\r\n\r\nAs a result `len(running_batch.reqs)` — logged as `#running-req`, exported as the `num_running_reqs` gauge, consumed by `/v1/loads` — grows monotonically for the whole run and over-reports the worker's load.\r\n\r\nThis is not limited to any special flag: `is_mixed_chunk = chunked_prefill_size is not None and enable_mixed_chunk`, and `enable_mixed_chunk` defaults to `False`, so the `else` branch is the common path. (The earlier #23895 framed this as `return_logprob=True`-specific; that PR is stale — it calls `filter_batch(v1_spec_info_filtered=True)`, a kwarg that no longer exists.)\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nAdd the missing `running_batch.filter_batch()` to the `else` branch of `_get_new_batch_prefill_raw()` in `python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py`.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n         else:\r\n+            # The mixed-chunk path above filters running_batch before mixing it into\r\n+            # the prefill batch; without it, finished requests are never removed and\r\n+            # #running-req / num_running_reqs grows monotonically for the whole run.\r\n+            running_batch.filter_batch()\r\n             new_batch.decoding_reqs = None\r\n\r\nFixes #43961",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "hope1262946533"
            },
            "body": "Related issue: #43961\r\n\r\nThis PR is the fix for it: `_get_new_batch_prefill_raw()` was missing\r\n`running_batch.filter_batch()` on the non-mixed-chunk prefill path, so finished\r\nrequests stayed in `running_batch.reqs` and `#running-req` / `num_running_reqs`\r\n/ `/v1/loads` over-reported load. The one-line change adds the missing call so\r\nboth prefill paths behave consistently.\r\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-13T07:34:33Z",
